{
  "$schema": "./schema.json",
  "day": 7,
  "level": 1,
  "title": { "en": "LL and Y, B and V, CH", "es": "La elle, la i griega, la be, la uve y la che" },
  "objectives": [
    "Say ll and y the same way",
    "Say b and v the same way, softening between vowels",
    "Pronounce ch",
    "Ask how to say something in Spanish"
  ],
  "teach": [
    {
      "kind": "sound",
      "grapheme": "ll · y",
      "ipa": "ʝ",
      "tip": "In most of Spain today ll and y sound the same (this is called yeísmo). It's like the y in 'yes', with a bit more contact, and after a pause or n it can sound close to the j in 'jam'. Only the spelling is different.",
      "examples": ["la calle", "la playa", "yo", "la llave"]
    },
    { "kind": "note", "md": "**y** on its own (meaning *and*) and **y** at the end of a word are a vowel, [i]: **y**, **muy**, **hoy**." },
    {
      "kind": "sound",
      "grapheme": "b · v",
      "ipa": "b · β",
      "tip": "b and v are the same sound. After a pause or m/n, it's a firm b (vale, bien). Everywhere else, especially between vowels, the lips come close without closing (β). Never bite your lip for an English v.",
      "examples": ["vale", "bien", "el vino", "por favor"]
    },
    { "kind": "sound", "grapheme": "ch", "ipa": "tʃ", "tip": "As in 'church'.", "examples": ["mucho", "la leche", "el coche", "ocho"] },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "¿Cómo se dice esto en español?", "en": "How do you say this in Spanish?", "note": "Point at something and ask. It also works with an English word: ¿Cómo se dice 'fork'?" },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "Muchas gracias.", "en": "Thank you very much.", "note": "Muchas, not muchos, because gracias is feminine." }
  ],
  "vocab": [
    { "id": "como-se-dice", "es": "¿Cómo se dice…?", "en": "How do you say…?", "pos": "phrase", "ipa": "ˈkomo se ˈðiθe", "note": "¿Cómo se dice esto en español? = How do you say this in Spanish?", "tags": ["survival"] },
    { "id": "muchas-gracias", "es": "muchas gracias", "en": "thank you very much", "pos": "phrase", "ipa": "ˈmutʃas ˈɣɾaθjas", "tags": ["survival"] },
    { "id": "mucho", "es": "mucho", "en": "a lot, much", "pos": "adv", "ipa": "ˈmutʃo" },
    { "id": "yo", "es": "yo", "en": "I", "pos": "pron", "ipa": "ˈʝo" },
    { "id": "calle", "es": "la calle", "en": "the street", "pos": "noun", "gender": "f", "ipa": "ˈkaʝe" },
    { "id": "playa", "es": "la playa", "en": "the beach", "pos": "noun", "gender": "f", "ipa": "ˈplaʝa" },
    { "id": "llave", "es": "la llave", "en": "the key", "pos": "noun", "gender": "f", "ipa": "ˈʝaβe" },
    { "id": "vino", "es": "el vino", "en": "the wine", "pos": "noun", "gender": "m", "ipa": "ˈbino", "note": "Vino tinto = red wine; vino blanco = white wine." },
    { "id": "leche", "es": "la leche", "en": "the milk", "pos": "noun", "gender": "f", "ipa": "ˈletʃe", "note": "Café con leche (coffee with milk) is the standard coffee order in Spain." },
    { "id": "coche", "es": "el coche", "en": "the car", "pos": "noun", "gender": "m", "ipa": "ˈkotʃe", "note": "Latin America: el carro or el auto." }
  ],
  "exercises": [
